  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. Headings - h1 to h6</h2>
    <p>HTML has <b>6 headings</b>. <b>h1</b> is the biggest, <b>h6</b> is the smallest.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;h1&gt;</span><span class="text">This is Heading 1 - Biggest</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;h2&gt;</span><span class="text">This is Heading 2</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h2&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;h3&gt;</span><span class="text">This is Heading 3</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h3&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;h4&gt;</span><span class="text">This is Heading 4</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h4&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;h5&gt;</span><span class="text">This is Heading 5</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h5&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;h6&gt;</span><span class="text">This is Heading 6 - Smallest</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h6&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>2. Result:</h2>
    <div class="result">
      <h1 style="margin:5px 0">This is Heading 1 - Biggest</h1>
      <h2 style="margin:5px 0">This is Heading 2</h2>
      <h3 style="margin:5px 0">This is Heading 3</h3>
      <h4 style="margin:5px 0">This is Heading 4</h4>
      <h5 style="margin:5px 0">This is Heading 5</h5>
      <h6 style="margin:5px 0">This is Heading 6 - Smallest</h6>
    </div>
    <div class="note"><b>Rule:</b> Use <b>h1 only 1 time</b> on one page. For other headings, use h2, h3. This is best for Google / SEO.</div>
    <h2>3. Paragraph - &lt;p&gt;</h2>
    <p>To write normal text, we use <b>&lt;p&gt;</b> tag.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">My name is Ali. I am learning HTML.</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">This is my second paragraph.</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>4. Line Break - &lt;br&gt;</h2>
    <p>To go to a new line, we use <b>&lt;br&gt;</b>. It has <b>no closing tag</b>.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">Line 1</span><span class="tag">&lt;br&gt;</span><span class="text"> Line 2</span><span class="tag">&lt;br&gt;</span><span class="text"> Line 3</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result">Line 1<br>Line 2<br>Line 3</div>
    <h2>5. Horizontal Line - &lt;hr&gt;</h2>
    <p>To draw a line on the page, we use <b>&lt;hr&gt;</b>. It also has no closing tag.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;h2&gt;</span><span class="text">Section 1</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h2&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;hr&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;h2&gt;</span><span class="text">Section 2</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h2&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>6. Comment - &lt;!-- --&gt;</h2>
    <p>A comment is text that is <b>not visible in the browser</b>, it is only in the code for notes.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code><span class="com">&lt;!-- This is a comment, browser will not show it --&gt;</span></code></div>
    <h2>7. Full Example</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;h1&gt;</span><span class="text">My Blog</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;h2&gt;</span><span class="text">About Me</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h2&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">Hello! My name is Ali.</span><span class="tag">&lt;br&gt;</span><span class="text"> I love coding.</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;hr&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;h2&gt;</span><span class="text">My Hobby</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h2&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">I like to make websites.</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>8. Homework</h2>
    <p>Make your own small About Page: your name in h1, About in h2, 2 lines in p, and use hr in the middle.</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Tags to remember:</b><br>h1 to h6 = Headings &nbsp; | &nbsp; p = Paragraph &nbsp; | &nbsp; br = New Line &nbsp; | &nbsp; hr = Horizontal Line &nbsp; | &nbsp; &lt;!-- --&gt; = Comment</div>
